The attached image illustrates the dendrimer-like structure of phytoglycogen (PG) and its derivatives during the synthesis of Nano-11. The spherical particles feature a dense, highly branched internal structure, originating from a central point, characteristic of dendrimers. In Fig. 1 of the PDF, these diagrams are used sequentially to represent the initial phytoglycogen (PG), then phytoglycogen octenyl succinate (PG-OS) after reaction with octenyl succinic anhydride (OSA), and finally the positively charged PG-OS-CHPTAC (Nano-11) after further reaction with (3-chloro-2-hydroxypropyl)-trimethylammonium chloride (CHPTAC). This visual representation supports the understanding of Nano-11 as a functionalized, dendrimer-like alpha-D-glucan nanoparticle.